Missing or non-positive observations create gaps in the reference line. The orange line is a formula reference, not an intrinsic-value estimate or price target. It uses retrospective information and is not a point-in-time investment backtest.</p><h2>Prices, ranges, and dividends</h2><p>Weekly data retains the last available row in each week. Prefer validated split-only closes when supplied; otherwise the chart uses labeled Stooq adjusted closes as an approximation. The chart ends at the latest available price date. Company tables retain newer annual filings independently.</p><p><a href="/guides/fiscal-year-dividend-yield/">Fiscal-year dividend yield</a> uses an annual reported dividend and a historical year-end close. It is off by default on the chart.</p><p><a href="/sources/">Source dates and limitations</a> · <a href="/about/">Author and corrections</a></p>`],
     ["/sources/", "Data sources, dates, and limitations", "SEC filing sources, historical Stooq prices, S&P 500 membership provenance, and coverage limitations.", `<h1>Sources, dates & limitations</h1><h2>Financial and price snapshot</h2><p>The financial database was built ${built}. Exporting or rebuilding the website does not obtain newer financial data or prices. Each company page displays its latest fiscal period and price date separately.</p><p>Reported financial facts come from <a href="https://www.sec.gov/edgar/search/">SEC EDGAR</a> through <a href="https://www.sec.gov/search-filings/edgar-application-programming-interfaces">SEC Company Facts</a>. Company table links point to the original filing index. FCF is calculated from reported inputs; its source links identify operating cash flow and capex. The current public export does not include separate share-denominator provenance.</p><p>Historical adjusted closes come from <a href="https://stooq.com/">Stooq</a>. The prepared US price snapshot ends no later than May 8, 2026. It currently contains no validated split-only US closes. These prices and dividend yields based on them are labeled approximations; they should not be interpreted as exact unadjusted year-end quotes.</p><h2>S&P 500 membership and classifications</h2>${membership}${verified ? `<ul>${verified}</ul>` : ""}<p>Share classes remain separate directory entries. Unmatched tickers, issuer-identity mismatches, and missing supported metrics or prices are labeled as coverage gaps. Historical values can predate index admission; the site does not reconstruct historical index membership.</p><h2>Limits of interpretation</h2><p>Missing facts are unavailable, not zero. Filing amendments, taxonomy changes, incomplete split tags, and issuer-level rather than share-class-specific facts can affect comparability. Check linked filings, especially for issuers with multiple share classes. No unsupported class conversion is performed.</p><p>Annual totals are not quarterly or trailing-twelve-month measures. A missing dividend observation does not establish that the company paid no dividend. Price and financial histories may cover different dates. Formula references are retrospective and do not establish fair value, future performance, or a trading recommendation.</p><p>This is independent historical research, not investment advice or an exact reproduction of proprietary FAST Graphs calculations. <a href="/about/">Report a suspected error</a>.</p>`],
     ["/about/", "About Cheng and Stock Value Lens", "A free historical stock research tool maintained by Cheng. Contact us with questions or data corrections.", `<h1>About & contact</h1><p>Stock Value Lens is a free tool for exploring historical earnings, cash flow, dividends, and stock prices. No account or subscription is required, including for charts and CSV/PNG exports.</p><h2>Authorship</h2><p>Created and maintained by ${e(site.author)}. Company tables and factual summaries are generated automatically from stored financial observations and a sourced membership list. This process does not create independent company reporting or investment recommendations.</p><h2>Questions and corrections</h2><p>Email <a href="mailto:${e(site.contactEmail)}">${e(site.contactEmail)}</a>. For data corrections, include the ticker, fiscal period, metric, and a link to the relevant filing if available.</p><p><a href="/methodology/">Read the methodology</a> and <a href="/sources/">review data sources and limitations</a>. This is an independent research project, not investment advice.</p>`],
